  "body": "Part of #4023 and of K7 (#4027). It is delivered on `side/path-kernel` (AGENTS.md **Side branch**). It does not depend on the crate skeleton (#4055, PR #4123): it measures a finished toolpath, so it reads only the toolpath, the region and the stock.\n\n## Why\n\nThe switch-over proof of the record `docs/decisions/4024-path-kernel-design.md` needs each law of #4023 \"measured on the disc, the dog bone and `fig8.step`, old against new\". The measuring code and the readings of the OLD planners can be made now. The K7 suite then runs the same measures on the new planners.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Add one measuring module for tests (in the existing test helpers of `camcraft-motion`, next to `shape_mask`). For a generated toolpath it gives these readings, each as a number with the list of the places:\n   - lifts on one level, and for each lift whether a named reason is given;\n   - planar feeds that cross a planned cut or leave the region (a crossing);\n   - entries into material: each entry with its kind, and whether it starts in air, in a hole, in a cleared column, or in solid material;\n   - cuts above the engagement limit (the radial engagement against the stock that is left), with the worst value;\n   - fallbacks: each note that says that a different plan was used.\n2. Add a readings test for each phase-1 kind on the three parts where the kind applies, with Inside and Outside where the kind has a start side. The test pins the readings of the OLD planner as they are today (a table in the test, not a pass/fail law). A reading that breaks a law is not a failure of this issue: it is the fact that the kernel must improve. Mark each such reading in the table.\n3. Use `fig8.step` only (the tracked public fixture). Never read the private project files in `testdata/models/`.\n4. Keep each test under the 60 s debug budget, or use the heavy lane with a light twin by the rules.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe measuring module has unit tests on hand-made toolpaths with known readings. The readings table of the old planners is in the PR body, kind by kind, and is pinned by tests on the side branch. No planner code changes.\n",
